      "url": "https://www.space.com/space-exploration/launches-spacecraft/spacex-moves-starship-flight-15-booster-to-launch-pad-for-squeeze-test-ahead-of-epic-double-catch-attempt-photos",
      "title": "SpaceX prepares Starship Flight 15 for first attempt to catch both stages",
      "content_html": "SpaceX moved Super Heavy Booster 22 to the launch mount at its Starbase facility in South Texas on Nov. 10 ahead of a Nov. 13 Starship test flight that will attempt to catch both the booster and the Ship upper stage with the launch tower’s mechanical arms. The 75-minute launch window is scheduled to open at 4:45 p.m. local time, subject to regulatory approval.\n\nThe booster is due to return about 6½ minutes after liftoff; Ship is scheduled to return roughly 22 hours later after deploying 26 Starlink V3 satellites and completing about 14 orbits. SpaceX has caught Super Heavy boosters three times but has never attempted to catch Ship, which must re-enter from orbit. The company will proceed with Ship’s return only if its systems meet the flight team’s criteria; otherwise, it plans an ocean landing.",
